Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.32,0:00:04.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Fourth track: data assimilation,\Nmerging a model with a few measurements.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.81,0:00:09.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Learned priors came in through compressed\Nlatent spaces, then diffusion models.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.66,0:00:14.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}And a library now plugs deep networks into\NKalman filters and variational methods.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.60,0:00:20.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}We found no diffusion prior used\Nthis way for conducting fluids.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.43,0:00:23.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Near a flip, the answer\Nhas two polarities,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.58,0:00:28.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}and a prior that ignores the\Nmirror could bias it toward one.
